    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0529" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5017/5–646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-09T18:00:00-04:00">May 9, 1946—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>605. Reurtel 835 May 6. Note recently received from Brazilian Embassy states
                    Brazilian Govt through DNC would place at disposal of US market 400,000 bags
                    coffee per month for 6 months at 3 cents above <pb facs="0530" n="512"
                        xml:id="pg512"/> present US ceilings in return for elimination of price
                    ceilings. This differs from info you received from Minister Vidigal concerning
                    sales of DNC coffee. Would appreciate your comments this offer.</p>
                <p>Coffee Board Price Committee discussing possible elimination price ceilings with
                    OPA.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
